description:
Implement a `Container` class that acts as a dependency injection container with singleton scope.

- `register(token, factory)` — registers a factory function for a string token
- `resolve(token)` — calls the factory (passing the container) and returns the instance; subsequent calls return the **same** instance (singleton)
- Throws an `Error` if `resolve` is called for an unregistered token

**Example:**
```js
const c = new Container();
c.register('logger', () => ({ log: (m) => console.log(m) }));
c.register('app', (container) => ({ logger: container.resolve('logger') }));
const app = c.resolve('app');
app.logger.log('hello'); // hello
c.resolve('app') === app; // true — singleton
```

